{
  "name": "nist_sp_800_53",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "cprt_framework_version",
      "value": "SP_800_53_5_2_0"
    },
    {
      "tag": "publication_date",
      "value": "2025-08"
    },
    {
      "tag": "oscal_content_tag",
      "value": "v1.6.0"
    },
    {
      "tag": "oscal_content_commit",
      "value": "f0de6d8d8c059d374f15e0ae07508d82e370fc1d"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of the security and privacy controls that NIST Special Publication 800-53, Revision 5, defines at Release 5.2.0: its twenty control families, their controls and control enhancements, each with its statement, discussion, organization-defined parameters, related controls and references; the assessment objectives and methods that SP 800-53A gives each control; and the four control baselines of SP 800-53B.",
  "title": "NIST SP 800-53 Security and Privacy Controls, Release 5.2.0",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the release of Revision 5 that the catalog carries, 5.2.0 of August 2025, and publication_date is that release's date; Revision 5 itself was published in September 2020 and updated in December 2020. source is the publication's digital object identifier. NIST's Cybersecurity and Privacy Reference Tool names the same release SP_800_53_5_2_0, and the catalog and the four baseline profiles NIST publishes for it in usnistgov/oscal-content are copied to src/nist_sp_800_53/schema/oscal-content/ at the tag and commit in the annotations. scripts/check_upstream_release.py reads the same pins and reports when NIST publishes a newer edition or changes a copied file. The release tags are the schema's own versions.",
    "SP 800-53, SP 800-53A and SP 800-53B are works of the United States Government and are not subject to copyright in the United States. The descriptions here are this project's own words; NIST's text of each control, parameter, objective and method stays in the catalog copy.",
    "NIST's catalog renders each family as an OSCAL group, each control and control enhancement as an OSCAL control, each statement, discussion, assessment objective and assessment method as a part, each organization-defined parameter as a parameter, each reference as a back-matter resource, and each baseline as a profile. The broad_mappings name those lmodel/oscal classes."
  ],
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53r5",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/nist-sp-800-53",
    "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/53/r5/upd1/final",
    "https://csrc.nist.gov/News/2025/nist-releases-revision-to-sp-800-53-controls",
    "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53Ar5",
    "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53B",
    "https://github.com/usnistgov/oscal-content/tree/v1.6.0/nist.gov/SP800-53/rev5"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-sp-800-53",
  "version": "5.2.0",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "prefixes": [
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "linkml",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/linkml/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "nist_sp_800_53",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-sp-800-53/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "oscal",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/oscal/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "schema",
      "prefix_reference": "http://schema.org/"
    },
